1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,161
Afternoon tea consists of several elements.
下午茶由几个部分组成。

2
00:00:03,161 --> 00:00:12,881
One of them is of course the tea itself, followed by finger sandwiches, usually with cucumber, salmon, eggs and chicken and curry sauce.
其中当然有茶，然后是小份三明治，常见馅料有黄瓜、三文鱼、鸡蛋和咖喱鸡肉。

3
00:00:12,881 --> 00:00:23,431
Accompanied by two canapes per person, scones with lemon curd cream, strawberry jam and clotted cream.
每人还配两份小点心，司康则搭配柠檬酱、草莓果酱和凝脂奶油。

4
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:32,251
And finally a selection of bite sized cakes and pastry.
最后还有一些一口大小的蛋糕和酥点。

5
00:00:32,261 --> 00:00:35,931
The daily afternoon tea is a highlight at the five star luxury hotel.
每日的下午茶是这家五星级酒店的一大特色。

6
00:00:35,941 --> 00:00:41,511
Traditionally guests start with a glass of champagne.
按照片中介绍，客人通常先喝一杯香槟。

7
00:00:41,521 --> 00:00:51,211
While we're enjoying the champagne, we'll be having our first course, which just the finger sandwiches.
享用香槟时，会端上第一道小三明治。

8
00:00:51,221 --> 00:00:56,681
Award winning pastry chef Nikola Ushe and his team make hundreds of these sandwiches every day.
片中的获奖糕点师和团队每天制作数百份这样的三明治。

9
00:00:56,681 --> 00:01:00,401
To maximize efficiency he uses some tricks of the trade.
为了提高效率，他会用一些行内的小技巧。

10
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:06,941
Activity which are ready to be sliced together.
这些三明治可以放在一起切。

11
00:01:06,941 --> 00:01:13,740
And the reason to slice them together to allow the sandwich to be tightly packed together to have a neat finish.
一起切能让三明治更紧实，切面也更整齐。

12
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:20,031
Now as you can see, this creates some beautiful colored layers which are quite visually eye catching.
可以看到，这样会形成漂亮的彩色层次，视觉上很吸引人。

13
00:01:20,041 --> 00:01:26,380
It wouldn't be afternoon tea without the actual tea, and guests have 28 varieties to choose from.
下午茶自然少不了茶，片中客人有二十八种茶可选。

14
00:01:26,380 --> 00:01:31,781
The most popular of which is a black tea produced especially for the hotel, the Savoy breakfast tea.
片中介绍，最受欢迎的是专为酒店制作的早餐红茶。

15
00:01:31,781 --> 00:01:35,571
And following tea drinking etiquette is strongly recommended.
原片还建议了解饮茶礼仪。

16
00:01:35,581 --> 00:01:40,361
We don't stir the tea like this. You go up and down.
茶匙不要这样搅动，示范的方法是上下轻移。

17
00:01:40,361 --> 00:01:46,260
And as well to make sure to not cling your teaspoon at the edges to not make any noise.
也尽量别让茶匙碰到杯沿发出声音。

18
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:48,941
And of course we don't lick the teaspoon.
当然，也不要舔茶匙。

19
00:01:48,941 --> 00:01:52,301
But of course rules are there meant to be broken.
不过，规则有时也可以灵活一点。

20
00:01:52,301 --> 00:02:00,631
Do not be scared because you can just be who you are during afternoon tea and enjoy your maybe special occasion.
不用紧张，享用下午茶时自然做自己，好好享受这次特别的聚会。

21
00:02:00,671 --> 00:02:09,012
The tradition of afternoon tea dates back to 1840 and was invented by the Duchess of Bedford, a lady in waiting to Queen Victoria.
片中说，下午茶传统可追溯到一八四〇年，与贝德福德公爵夫人有关，她曾侍奉维多利亚女王。

22
00:02:09,012 --> 00:02:13,632
She thought, she thought there was too much of a gap between lunch and dinner.
她觉得午餐和晚餐之间隔得太久。

23
00:02:13,632 --> 00:02:20,292
So she asked her surface to in the afternoon to make sandwiches, to make scones, to make cakes.
于是，她请人在下午准备三明治、司康和蛋糕。

24
00:02:20,292 --> 00:02:26,592
And she really enjoyed it. She was eating it and she loved it, so she started inviting her friends for it as well.
她很喜欢，后来也开始邀请朋友一起享用。

25
00:02:26,592 --> 00:02:30,012
So this then became, all her friends came over, and this became a tradition.
朋友们陆续来做客，这就慢慢成了一项传统。

26
00:02:30,012 --> 00:02:38,422
By the time the Savoy Hotel opened in 1889, afternoon tea was always, well, was already a well established tradition.
片中说，酒店在一八八九年开业时，下午茶已经是成熟的传统。

27
00:02:38,432 --> 00:02:44,531
The Savoy was built as London's first luxury hotel and maintains its status as such.
原片将萨沃伊介绍为伦敦早期的豪华酒店，并说它一直保持这一定位。

28
00:02:44,531 --> 00:02:48,552
Since day one, afternoon tea has been an institution of its own.
从开业起，下午茶就逐渐成了这里独具特色的一部分。

29
00:02:48,552 --> 00:02:54,602
And the highlight of the tea ceremony has to be the etagere with cakes and scones.
茶席的亮点，当然还有放着蛋糕和司康的多层点心架。

30
00:02:54,612 --> 00:03:05,792
And we are baking them throughout the day every half an hour to make sure then they arrive piping hot and just at the right texture and temperature at the table.
我们全天每半小时烤一批，确保上桌时热腾腾，口感和温度都合适。

31
00:03:05,792 --> 00:03:09,612
How to eat scones is a hotly debated topic in England.
片中说，在英格兰，司康怎么吃是个常被热烈讨论的话题。

32
00:03:09,612 --> 00:03:14,552
The most divisive question, what comes first, jam or clotted cream?
最容易引发争论的是：先抹果酱，还是先抹凝脂奶油？

33
00:03:14,552 --> 00:03:19,102
So far there is no law against either.
至少到原片讲述时，两种吃法都没人禁止。

34
00:03:19,112 --> 00:03:25,822
Last but not least, the cakes are served.
最后，同样不能少的是蛋糕。

35
00:03:25,832 --> 00:03:31,872
And such but cakes are the most important elements, and are also like a pellet cleanser.
蛋糕也是重要的一部分，片中还提到清新味觉的收尾。

36
00:03:31,872 --> 00:03:40,622
Something with fresh fruits, which after the scones, after the sandwiches, after the cakes, is a nice refreshing touch.
吃过司康、三明治和蛋糕后，来一点鲜果，会增添清爽的感觉。
